 "note": "Mutants of the cap of starting ants of an online room (OnlineLimits::kMaxStartAnts = 1,000, all four colors together) and of the weight of a match (the most of the places of its cells and of its ants, one for every started 400 ants), for tools/mutate.py (docs/WORKFLOW.md, 'Mutation checks'). Run from the checkout with a configured build folder: python3 tools/mutate.py tests/data/online_ants_cap_mutants.json --keep-going --jobs 1 --timeout 1500. Every mutant must be caught: each breaks one rule of docs/SERVER.md ('Online size limit', 'Starting ants') or docs/MAP_SUBMISSIONS.md ('The online size limit'). The web side (the Play this map dialog's refusal and the picker's chip) is in tests/data/mapmaker_play_mutants.json (play_cap_*) and tests/scripts/test_web_map_picker.py. Not listed on purpose: three second locks behind a first one that a test does reach: the check in Room::start_lobby and in the lobby's START (Room::update) behind choose_map, load_map and build_room (no door of the manager makes a Room on a map over the cap, so no test can start one), the ants check in the history's approved-map callback behind the feeder's own load_level (the two calls of load_level are listed: a new file, MP2.3, and the stats of an older record, MP2.4).",
